From: drw@BOURBAKI.MIT.EDU
Subject: POLI: May my sister visit me?

   From: pmetzger@shearson.com (Perry E. Metzger)

   Can someone tell me how an immigrant can possibly be construed to be
   committing a tort by his immigration?

   I really can't imagine a mechanism that would keep immigrants out of
   anything but the smallest of communities, and at that level even the
   xenophobes must see that their foolishness can get them nowhere as
   the jobs that they are "losing" are merely going to the next town.

The basic idea is that all landowners would cede some measure of
control over their land to the PPL.  This could be a group as small as
a single building, or as large as a present nation.  Then the
governing body of PPL simply decrees that landowners are not allowed
to permit anybody who is not a "legal resident" onto their property.
At that point, people who are not "legal residents" are trespassors,
and can be forcibly removed.

To make it work, you have to have a PPL that covers enough land that
it can get reasonable control over the job market in its territory.
So a single building is too small, but something the size of a
metropolitan area or a state is large enough.

Dale

